{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789766439,"nonce":"bG1CqX8Dov5qaj9IQzu87jDcCXc=","title":"a store to a Null\u003cInt\u003e field lands at a byte offset and tramples its neighbours","message":"`var n:Null\u003cInt\u003e` in a class: `n = 7` in the constructor turned a sibling\n`var a = 11` into 10; `n = null` zeroed it. With `var kid = new Child()`\nbefore it, `kid.v` read 1024 or 0 and `Reflect.field(this, \"kid\")` crashed\non a pointer whose low three bytes were gone. Any class that writes a\n`Null\u003cscalar\u003e` field is affected; only shows once the field's index is\nsmall enough to overlap real slots (index 3 writes bytes 3..11: the top\nbyte of the header and the low three of field 1).\n\nMechanism: a boxed `Null\u003cT\u003e` field's IrType is `Ptr(U8)`, and every tier's\nGEP rule scaled `Ptr(U8 | I8)` by one byte (\"byte-pointer types\"), 8 bytes\nfor everything else. Loads and stores of the field agreed with each other,\nso the field itself read back right while its neighbours were corrupted.\nEvery byte-buffer emitter spells its pointer `Ptr(I8)`; no emitter passes\n`Ptr(U8)` on purpose. Fix: only `*i8` is byte-addressed (LLVM, Cranelift,\ninterpreter, C, WASM).\n\nFound on the way, same path: the field-init lowering in the constructor\n(`expr/functions.rs`) stored the initializer raw — `n:Null\u003cInt\u003e = 44` put\n44 in a slot every reader unboxes (fault=0x2c). It boxes to the field type\nnow, as an assignment does.\n\nAlso in this change, from the reproducer that led here (74b3bef): a class\nfield's RTTI `ParamType` had no Array/anon kind, so `Reflect.field`/`d.f`\nhanded back Array and anonymous fields as an Int box holding the pointer,\nand a class field the same way. `IrField` carries a shape now\n(Class/Array/Anonymous) and the RTTI boxes by it; the call boundary\nunboxes String/Array/anon formals by tag.\n\nReproducer: /tmp/probe/p9217/N1.hx, B9.hx; fixture\nhaxe-conformance/regressions/NullableFieldSlots.hx.","files":null}]}